1
00:00:00,024 --> 00:00:06,660
(Q31) Well, l've been talking to managers in a number of businesses, and reading surveys about the future of management.

2
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:15,403
And what l'm going to present in this seminar is a few ideas about how the activity is likely to change in the next ten years.

3
00:00:15,403 --> 00:00:22,041
It isn't a scientific, statistical analysis - just some ideas for us to discuss.

4
00:00:22,041 --> 00:00:36,341
[Q31答案句] One area I want to mention is business markets, and I'm sure a really significant development will be a major increase in competition, with companies from all round the world trying to sell similar products.

5
00:00:36,341 --> 00:00:49,154
(Q32) Consumers will have much more choice - for instance, food products sold in Australia might be manufactured in the USA, China, Finland and dozens of other countries.

6
00:00:49,154 --> 00:00:57,628
[Q32答案句] At the same time, mergers and takeovers mean that governments are actually losing power to major global corporations.

7
00:00:57,628 --> 00:01:05,653
(Q33) We can probably all think of companies that exert a great deal of influence, which may be good for consumers.

8
00:01:05,653 --> 00:01:18,211
[Q33答案句] A third point I want to make about markets is that in the rapidly expanding economies, such as India, China, Brazil and Russia, demand is growing very fast.

9
00:01:18,211 --> 00:01:22,487
This is putting pressure on resources all over the world.

10
00:01:22,487 --> 00:01:27,901
(Q34) I think businesses are becoming more open to external influences.

11
00:01:27,901 --> 00:01:34,696
[Q34答案句] In particular, companies are consulting customers more and more before making their business decisions.

12
00:01:34,696 --> 00:01:44,038
(Q35) Companies are finding out what they want and providing it, instead of making products and then trying to sell them, which is the model of years ago.

13
00:01:44,038 --> 00:01:54,854
Another influence is that concerns about the environment will force manufacturers to extend product lifecycles, to reduce the amount of pollution and waste.

14
00:01:54,854 --> 00:02:00,695
[Q35答案句] And in some cases. regulation will need to be strengthened.

15
00:02:00,695 --> 00:02:08,277
(Q36) Many societies are much more fluid and democratic, and the structure of companies is changing to reflect that.

16
00:02:08,277 --> 00:02:16,075
[Q36答案句] I think we're going to see a greater emphasis within companies on teams created with a specific project in mind.

17
00:02:16,075 --> 00:02:21,523
(Q37) And when they're completed, the teams will be disbanded and new ones formed.

18
00:02:21,523 --> 00:02:38,757
More and more people see work as simply one part of their lifestyle, and not the most important one, and as the workforce is shrinking in some countries, businesses are having to compete for staff instead of being able to choose among a lot of applicants.

19
00:02:38,757 --> 00:03:00,684
[Q37答案句] Typical examples that will attract and retain staff are traditional ones like flexible hours and - something that has been made possible by advances in technology - remote working, with people based at their home, abroad, or almost anywhere they choose.

20
00:03:00,684 --> 00:03:05,849
(Q38) Management styles will almost certainly continue to change.

21
00:03:05,849 --> 00:03:11,056
Senior managers will require a lot more than the efficiency that they've always needed.

22
00:03:11,056 --> 00:03:26,201
[Q38答案句] Above all they'll need great skills in leadership, so that their organisation can initiate and respond to change in a fast-moving world, where they face lots of competing requirements and potential conflicts.

23
00:03:26,201 --> 00:03:33,510
(Q39) In most of the world, the senior managers of large businesses are mainly men in their fifties and sixties.

24
00:03:33,510 --> 00:03:45,708
[Q39答案句] The predominant style of management will almost certainly become more consultative and collaborative, caused above all, by more women moving into senior management positions.

25
00:03:45,708 --> 00:03:51,090
(Q40) Many of the changes are influenced by developments in the wider economy.

26
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:58,325
The traditional emphasis of business was manufacturing, and of course the service sector is very important.

27
00:03:58,325 --> 00:04:06,062
But we shouldn't overlook the growing financial contribution of IP, that is, intellectual property.

28
00:04:06,062 --> 00:04:16,276
Some books and films generate enormous sums from the sale of related DVDs, music, games, clothes, and so on.

29
00:04:16,276 --> 00:04:28,522
Another point I'd like to make is that although l've been talking about companies, one trend that they have to face is the move away from people working for the same employer for years.

30
00:04:28,522 --> 00:04:39,636
[Q40答案句] Instead, more and more people are becoming self-employed, to gain the freedom and control over their lives that they're unlikely to get from being employed.

31
00:04:39,636 --> 00:04:42,136
OK, well that's all I want to say, so let's open it up for discussion.

